<p>This week surveys the opening chapters of biblical history, beginning with the creation accounts in Genesis and continuing through the Patriarchal period, the Exodus from Egypt, and the covenant formation of Israel as a nation. We situate these events within the broader context of the ancient Near East, paying attention to the great civilizations of Mesopotamia, Egypt, and Canaan that formed the backdrop of the biblical narrative.</p>

